# CI (`.github/**`)

- Reuse `.github/actions/setup-playwright` (pnpm, Node LTS, frozen lockfile). API-only jobs pass no `browsers` input, so no browser is downloaded. Do not copy its steps into workflows.
- The API under test is started by Playwright's `webServer` (`API_SERVER_COMMAND` / `API_SERVER_CWD` / `API_SERVER_READY_URL`), never with a backgrounded `&` step. The workflow only provisions what that command needs (checkout of the app, its toolchain, its dependencies). In CI the server always starts fresh (`reuseExistingServer: false`).
- Reporters in CI come from `playwright.config.ts` (`blob` + `github`); every workflow merges `blob-report` into HTML with `playwright merge-reports` and uploads `playwright-report/`.
- Three strategies, one file each: `playwright-serial.yml` (`--workers=1`, manual), `playwright-parallel.yml` (default workers, PR = `--grep @smoke`, push = full), `playwright-sharded.yml` (matrix `--shard=i/n`, separate `merge-reports` job, nightly). Pick with `playwright-ci`'s strategy guide. Each shard starts its own server.
- Secrets: `API_USER_EMAIL`, `API_USER_PASSWORD`, `API_ADMIN_EMAIL`, `API_ADMIN_PASSWORD`. Variables with defaults: `API_BASE_URL`, `API_SERVER_*`. Never commit values.
- `lint.yml` runs `pnpm lint` on every push and PR; it is the blocking quality gate.
- Validate YAML before committing (`ruby -ryaml -e 'YAML.load_file(ARGV[0])' <file>`).
